# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision Update<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
The purpose of this research plan is to investigate the impact of sustainable fashion practices on the environment and human well-being. The following sections outline the refined research questions, methods, and data collection plan.<br>
<br>
## Refined Research Questions<br>
<br>
1. What are the most effective ways to reduce textile waste in the fashion industry?<br>
2. How can sustainable fashion practices improve air quality and mitigate climate change?<br>
3. What are the social implications of adopting sustainable fashion practices?<br>
<br>
## Methods<br>
<br>
This research will employ a mixed-methods approach, combining both qualitative and quantitative data collection methods.<br>
<br>
* Qualitative: In-depth interviews with industry experts and stakeholders to gather insights on best practices and challenges.<br>
* Quantitative: Analysis of existing literature and data on textile waste, air quality, and climate change.<br>
<br>
## Data Collection Plan<br>
<br>
Data will be collected through the following sources:<br>
<br>
* Industry reports and publications<br>
* Academic journals and research papers<br>
* Online surveys and questionnaires with industry experts and stakeholders<br>
* In-depth interviews with key informants<br>
<br>
## Analysis Plan<br>
<br>
Data will be analyzed using descriptive statistics and thematic analysis to identify patterns and trends.<br>
<br>
## Conclusion<br>
<br>
This revised research plan incorporates feedback from industry experts and outlines a clear approach for data collection and analysis. The refined research questions and methods will provide valuable insights into the impact of sustainable fashion practices on the environment and human well-being.<br>
